<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Document Conversion</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif; /* Using serif fonts as primary */
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  /* Basic styling to mimic layout structure */
  .header-info { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 12pt; }
  .main-content { display: flex; gap: 60px; }
  .column { flex: 1; }
  .signature-block { margin-top: 50px; }
  .address-block { margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .section-title { font-weight: bold; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  td { padding: 5px 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="page">
  <div class="header-info">
    <div>
      <span data-field="sender_name">{{ sender_name }}</span><br>
      <span data-field="sender_address_line1">{{ sender_address_line1 }}</span><br>
      <span data-field="sender_address_line2">{{ sender_address_line2 }}</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span data-field="date">{{ date }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="main-content">
    <div class="column">
      <p>In the light of your editorial position on the <span data-field="topic_name">{{ topic_name }}</span>, I believe that you and your readers will be interested in excerpts from a letter which I have sent to <span data-field="recipient_name">{{ recipient_name }}</span>, a former fellow Marine of Lee Harvey Oswald.</p>
      <p>As I understand the facts, you were unable to identify John Reese the Anaheim resident with whom Lee Harvey Oswald conversed in <span data-field="location">{{ location }}</span> during the time when you were both in service, thus frustrating a plan to charge Heinzel with perjury and/or conspiracy if he denied such conversations with Oswald. Carrison, who had considered you a "friendly witness," then placed you under suspicion of clandestine association with Oswald during his residence in New Orleans in 1963 and charged, privately, that you were an agent of the CIA. He produced before the New Orleans grand jury a woman who identified you more than four years after the alleged "fact"—as the man she had seen together with Oswald in New Orleans cafe in the summer of fall of 1963.</p>
      <p>I am further informed that you do not have means to ensure a proper legal representation against charges which appear to result from our right harassment and entrapment, on wholly false grounds, by an unscrupulous and vindictive prosecutor who is pressing an uninformed, irresponsible, and often lunatic "investigation" into the Kennedy assassination which threatens to cast into utter disrepute all challenges to the Warren Report, including those which are legitimate, impartial, and scholarly.</p>
      <p>Such flagrant abuse of trust and such ruthless action against innocent bystanders can only arouse my disgust and indignation—the more so when committed in the name of truth and justice, and be certified by the critics of the Warren Report who supposedly were wholly committed to high principles and the strictest ethical standards. I am enclosing herewith my check for one hundred dollars to assist you in meeting legal costs in defending yourself against spurious and malicious charges which amount to outright frame-up. I am also sending copies of this letter to a number of persons, including reporters and editors, in the hope that they will be willing to call public attention to your plight and to assist you with funds to meet the fees of your defense. You may feel sure that I will use every opportunity which presents itself to make the facts known and to enlist support.</p>
      <div class="signature-block">
        <p>Sincerely,</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 50px;">
          <span data-field="sender_signature_name">{{ sender_signature_name }}</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="column">
      <div class="address-block">
        <p>The Minority of One</p>
        <p><span data-field="address_line1">{{ address_line1 }}</span></p>
        <p><span data-field="address_line2">{{ address_line2 }}</span></p>
        <p><span data-field="address_line3">{{ address_line3 }}</span></p>
      </div>

      <div class="section-title">AN ALLEGED PACIFIST ON GEORGIA</div>
      <p>Appears to be a letter from <span data-field="sender_name_2">{{ sender_name_2 }}</span>, a resident of <span data-field="city_2">{{ city_2 }}</span>, <span data-field="state_2">{{ state_2 }}</span>. The letter discusses the political climate and the role of pacifism in the current events.</p>
      <p>The author expresses concerns about the direction of the country and the perceived lack of moral guidance from leadership. They advocate for a return to fundamental principles and a greater emphasis on individual conscience.</p>

      <div class="section-title">A VITAMIN</div>
      <p>This section appears to be a brief commentary on the necessity of certain elements—metaphorically or literally—for societal health. It suggests that without these elements, the body politic suffers.</p>
      <p>The text implies a need for balance and diverse viewpoints to maintain equilibrium.</p>

      <div class="section-title">THE SOLUTION AVAILABLE FOR VIETNAM</div>
      <p>Newly concerned citizens, Right-wing columnists, and Administration officials continue to urge the discontents to propose a solution to the war. I would like to say that for at least six years now we have been offering good and sound solutions, but no one has been listening.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="header-info">
    <div>
      <span data-field="sender_name_3">{{ sender_name_3 }}</span><br>
      <span data-field="sender_address_line1_3">{{ sender_address_line1_3 }}</span><br>
      <span data-field="sender_address_line2_3">{{ sender_address_line2_3 }}</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span data-field="date_3">{{ date_3 }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="main-content">
    <div class="column">
      <div class="section-title">THE MINORITY OF ONE</div>
      <p>P. O. BOX <span data-field="zip_code_3">{{ zip_code_3 }}</span>, <span data-field="city_3">{{ city_3 }}</span>, <span data-field="state_3">{{ state_3 }}</span></p>
      <p>ENTER/REVIEW MY SUBSCRIPTION FOR <span data-field="period_3">{{ period_3 }}</span></p>
      <table>
        <tr>
          <td><input type="radio" name="subscription" value="1"></td>
          <td><span data-field="price_1">{{ price_1 }}</span></td>
          <td><span data-field="period_option_1">{{ period_option_1 }}</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><input type="radio" name="subscription" value="2"></td>
          <td><span data-field="price_2">{{ price_2 }}</span></td>
          <td><span data-field="period_option_2">{{ period_option_2 }}</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><input type="radio" name="subscription" value="3"></td>
          <td><span data-field="price_3">{{ price_3 }}</span></td>
          <td><span data-field="period_option_3">{{ period_option_3 }}</span></td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <p>Student subscription at <span data-field="student_price">{{ student_price }}</span> (Foreign: <span data-field="foreign_price">{{ foreign_price }}</span>).</p>

      <div class="section-title">Address</div>
      <div class="address-block">
        <p>Name: <span data-field="name_3">{{ name_3 }}</span></p>
        <p>Address: <span data-field="address_3">{{ address_3 }}</span></p>
        <p>City & State: <span data-field="city_state_3">{{ city_state_3 }}</span></p>
        <p>Zip: <span data-field="zip_3">{{ zip_3 }}</span></p>
      </div>

      <div class="section-title">Other Subscriptions</div>
      <table>
        <tr>
          <td><input type="checkbox" name="other_sub"></td>
          <td>I request a copy of <span data-field="other_sub_name_1">{{ other_sub_name_1 }}</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><input type="checkbox" name="other_sub"></td>
          <td>I request a copy of <span data-field="other_sub_name_2">{{ other_sub_name_2 }}</span></td>
        </tr>
      </table>

      <div class="section-title">Payment Information</div>
      <p>Make check payable to <span data-field="payable_to">{{ payable_to }}</span>.</p>
      <p>Enclosed is my contribution of <span data-field="contribution_amount">{{ contribution_amount }}</span> to your publication fund.</p>

      <div class="section-title">Contact Information</div>
      <div class="address-block">
        <p>Name: <span data-field="name_4">{{ name_4 }}</span></p>
        <p>Address: <span data-field="address_4">{{ address_4 }}</span></p>
        <p>City & State: <span data-field="city_state_4">{{ city_state_4 }}</span></p>
        <p>Zip: <span data-field="zip_4">{{ zip_4 }}</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="column">
      <div class="section-title">GARRISON VICTIM</div>
      <p>In the light of your editorial position on the <span data-field="topic_name_2">{{ topic_name_2 }}</span>, I believe that you and your readers will be interested in excerpts from a letter which I have sent to <span data-field="recipient_name_2">{{ recipient_name_2 }}</span>, a former fellow Marine of Lee Harvey Oswald.</p>
      <p>As I understand the facts, you were unable to identify John Reese the Anaheim resident with whom Lee Harvey Oswald conversed in <span data-field="location_2">{{ location_2 }}</span> during the time when you were both in service, thus frustrating a plan to charge Heinzel with perjury and/or conspiracy if he denied such conversations with Oswald. Carrison, who had considered you a "friendly witness," then placed you under suspicion of clandestine association with Oswald during his residence in New Orleans in 1963 and charged, privately, that you were an agent of the CIA. He produced before the New Orleans grand jury a woman who identified you more than four years after the alleged "fact"—as the man she had seen together with Oswald in New Orleans cafe in the summer of fall of 1963.</p>
      <p>I am further informed that you do not have means to ensure a proper legal representation against charges which appear to result from our right harassment and entrapment, on wholly false grounds, by an unscrupulous and vindictive prosecutor who is pressing an uninformed, irresponsible, and often lunatic "investigation" into the Kennedy assassination which threatens to cast into utter disrepute all challenges to the Warren Report, including those which are legitimate, impartial, and scholarly.</p>
      <p>Such flagrant abuse of trust and such ruthless action against innocent bystanders can only arouse my disgust and indignation—the more so when committed in the name of truth and justice, and be certified by the critics of the Warren Report who supposedly were wholly committed to high principles and the strictest ethical standards. I am enclosing herewith my check for one hundred dollars to assist you in meeting legal costs in defending yourself against spurious and malicious charges which amount to outright frame-up. I am also sending copies of this letter to a number of persons, including reporters and editors, in the hope that they will be willing to call public attention to your plight and to assist you with funds to meet the fees of your defense. You may feel sure that I will use every opportunity which presents itself to make the facts known and to enlist support.</p>
      <div class="signature-block">
        <p>Sincerely,</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 50px;">
          <span data-field="sender_signature_name_2">{{ sender_signature_name_2 }}</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>